      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e5619984444702227d7b0e1|full_name}: Some of us are actually anti-social or asocial or semi-social and I think that should be respected too.\nIt's not as simple as us ignoring people - as a semi-social person myself, I just don't have the social energy to be open and accepting of a thousand people at all times.\nI think any type of person who ends up friending en masse will have that problem (streamers, community owners, etc), but even anti-social people with few friends will get socially drained.\nMy fix here basically allows reclusive people like myself to more easily gate off the majority of our acquaintances while being more open to the select few we want to be open with.\nAs for the people who end up gated off, they can more easily filter us out of their list and find the friends more currently open at the time instead of having to manually filter through potentially hundreds of people on orange or busy or private worlds.\nAt some point reclusive people do come out of their shells. In the mean time, find other people who are more open.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
